nvdisplay: kern_gpu_t234d: configure for NVRM-only T194 operation

All HAL functions are resolved via compile-time macros to T234D variants.
Modify the T234D functions to serve T194 (Xavier) as NVRM resource
manager only. Strip display subsystems from child lists and set T194
chip identity.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform-specific]
Signed-off-by: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
--- a/nvdisplay/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/arch/t23x/kern_gpu_t234d.c
+++ b/nvdisplay/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/arch/t23x/kern_gpu_t234d.c
@@ -34,8 +34,6 @@
 #include "g_allclasses.h"
 #include <nv_arch.h>
 
-#include "swref/published/t23x/t234/dev_fuse.h"
-
 /*!
  * @brief fill in the GPU ID information
  */
@@ -45,8 +43,8 @@
     OBJGPU   *pGpu
 )
 {
-    pGpu->chipInfo.platformId       = GPU_ARCHITECTURE_T23X;
-    pGpu->chipInfo.implementationId = GPU_IMPLEMENTATION_T234D;
+    pGpu->chipInfo.platformId       = GPU_ARCHITECTURE_T19X;
+    pGpu->chipInfo.implementationId = GPU_IMPLEMENTATION_T194;
     pGpu->chipInfo.revisionId = 0;
 }
 
